cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ARB, cite the paper and the archived release below."
title: "Agent Recovery Bench: Measuring Whether Failures Are Detected Early and Repaired Reliably in Tool-Using and Multi-Agent Workflows"
abstract: >-
  ARB is a benchmark, dataset, deterministic harness and leaderboard protocol for failure
  detection and recovery in multi-step tool-using and multi-agent workflows. It contributes a
  seven-class failure taxonomy, four deterministic tool environments with state-verified
  outcomes, a controlled fault-injection harness with harm screening, and a four-way recovery
  comparison (no recovery, retry-only, rule-based, model-based) under a fixed price sheet.
